-time and high-level  dashboard for a more focused summary of  how a project or model is doing go to  1db dot me slash ai minus coffee minus  break to explore and interact with these  reports yourself and see how reports can  help you share your work with colleagues  around the world  okay so here's the news we have this  texture image generation model dalit2  from openai it's a diffusion model that  can take in text and produce an amazing  picture if you're interested in how  text-to-image diffusion models work  check out our previous videos on this  but now here's the catch dalit ii can  not only take insensible input text and  produce its best shots at an image from  this but no it can take in gibberish and  produce output that looks really good  and even more it seems like this  gibberish does mean something for the  model because the combination of  something that produces birds with  something that produces bugs in apoplos  reality realities eating contara chat  nyams lurikatanyonuns  gives images of birds eating bugs  is this language  no it's not as the authors have quickly  realized after announcing their findings  on twitter and changed their paper title  from secret language to secret  vocabulary  language has syntax and grammar but ali  too seems rather to respond at gibberish  words  so how did the authors find and generate  such examples  it seems like the discovery happened  while the authors were playing with the  text rendering capabilities of dali 2.  the model is already known to produce  very weird results on this  so they gave the model an input where it  had to produce text like two farmers  talking about vegetables with subtitles  and found that the produced text is not  as random as one might think this word  vikutez produces dishes with vegetables  and apoplo vesraetars produces birds  so the authors concluded that the  farmers must be talking about birds  messing with their vegetables in this  thread you can see other examples too  but what we see there and in the paper  are not really many examples and it is a  bit unclear on what the success rate of  this method is  sometimes it works sometimes it doesn't  as highlighted in this thread where only  4 out of 10 examples generate sports  from the word tibur even though like in  the farmer's examples those two men  speak about tibor which seems to be  about sports so why does this even  happen that tali2 generates good looking  pictures from gibberish  the authors make the fuzzy claim that  the model has internally developed a  hidden language  we mean vocabulary after being trained  on image text pairs  well this is not very specific so let's  look at the theories circulating on  twitter right now because there are a  few very interesting ones the first one  i saw was by yoshabach he points out  that the text generations are quite  inconsistent  in the paper the authors prompt dali too  with two whales talking about food with  subtitles but yo shabbat points out that  the secret words one gets from this are  different every time  so your shabbat goes on saying that the  secret words are just random strings  that sometimes point to consistent  regions in the embedding space  the model projects the samples into high  dimensional space and clusters  neighboring concepts then honestly i do  not get what the rest of the explanation  wants to say maybe you know so go to the  comments and explain it if you want  so here is miss coffee beans take on  this which  might be very different from the one in  this thread sorry  the model has a limited number of  parameters and for efficiency reasons it  needs to cluster the space of words well  so concepts that are related to one  another should be close in this space  since we are working with neural  networks the text is represented as  continuous vectors but surprise text is  discrete and is composed of words that  do not have an in between as continuous  vectors do and since the model always  must produce an output whatever the  input the in between words so gibberish  will also produce an output  as it turns out this is sometimes  consistent between the string input and  rendered text in the image how seldomly  this works and how inconsistent this is  is highlighted by another twitter user  who points out that the bug producing  prompt does not produce so many bugs or  pests after all since in these daily two  generations we also have animals like  deer and goats  still along the line of the discreetness  of language are the opinions that say  that the secret language is mostly due  to tokenizer effects since apodi de and  plo seide are families of birds each  with more than 100 species apple deforms  is the biggest order of birds with 400  and more species of birds  so the model has connected the apple and  plow subwords to words somebody else  found that one can infer some of these  subwords that will work with dali too by  looking at wikipedia  where  actinopterygie and placodermi are two  families of fish and then placo actin  fig  generates fish images  you know with neural networks sometimes  it is great input in garbage out  now it's gibberish in quality images out  and everybody freaks out  it's clear that we do not yet understand  these black boxes and unless some more  rigorous interpretability goes into  these models we will continue prompting  in the dark and we will hope for the  best it's important to highlight that as  long as we are surprised by this weird  way of communication from daddy to and  similar models we are also ignorant of  some security issues adversarial attacks  with these gibberish prompts as well as  not so gibberish prompts can trigger  unwanted behavior from others  circumventing filters on the allowed  inputs it's clear that so far these  models do not behave like humans would  expect them to and malicious humans  could take advantage of this  what do you think about this would you  be interested to enroll in miss coffee  beans dali 2 language classes  see you next time  [Music]  [Music]  you

